LOCAL MODIFICATIONS
-------------------

The vendored files are NOT verbatim, except examples/scheduled-send.html. Every file a patch
changes carries this line, in its own comment syntax, from patch 0001 on:

    Modified by the plans plugin. Upstream pin and local patches: plugins/plans/NOTICE.

The patches below apply on top of upstream, in this order. Each one assumes the ones before
it, so a later patch's context is the text an earlier one wrote.

-----BEGIN PATCHES-----
0001-modification-notices.patch
    Adds the modification notice above to every vendored file that a patch in this list
    changes: after the shebang in pack.mjs, at the top of htmlplan.js, htmlplan.css and
    blocks.md, and after the frontmatter of SKILL.md.
0002-plan-reference.patch
    Renames SKILL.md to references/plan.md, a reference the first-party doc skill loads for
    the plan kind. Strips the frontmatter, the $ARGUMENTS line and the Artifact-tool
    hand-over, makes its paths relative to the new location, and points the hand-over at
    the "Delivery policy" section of plans:publish.
0003-theme-tokens.patch
    Renames every runtime-owned custom property to --plans-*, including --d, --tr-depth and
    --top that htmlplan.js generates, and maps them onto T3's theme variables with the
    upstream colours as fixed fallbacks, so a page follows the host's theme. ink-3 reads
    --muted-foreground and sunk reads --muted; ink-2 and line-2 mix two host colours and
    purple stays fallback-only, since T3 has no match. Soft colours use T3's *-surface
    variables where they exist, else a 12% color-mix, with the upstream pairs under
    @supports. Text on a solid accent reads --primary-foreground. Mockup content keeps
    its own palette. The token block is shared byte for byte with skills/show/tokens.css.
0004-fragment-state.patch
    Moves the reader's state out of localStorage, which throws in the viewer's opaque-origin
    sandbox, into the URL fragment: #pl1.<base64url(UTF-8 JSON)>, then an optional
    ~<percent-encoded anchor>, written only by history.replaceState. In-page links scroll
    and rewrite only the anchor, reset keeps only the anchor, leaving the page flushes a
    pending save, and a link pasted into an open page reloads it to restore that link's
    state. A fragment over 32 KiB or JSON over 24 KiB is not written, and a persistent note
    asks the reader to copy their response. A malformed payload restores nothing. The pure
    codec is exported as HtmlPlan.fragment for the smoke.
0005-media-for-the-cli.patch
    Stops pack base64-inlining media. Local media stays a literal src to a file beside the
    page, which the plans CLI uploads at publish time. Each doc-shot gets a literal <img>
    child in place of its own src, so the CLI sees the screenshot, and the runtime adopts
    that child. Media resolves only inside the page's own folder, never under --root. pack
    refuses an escape, a missing or root-only file, remote media, a local .html src, a type
    outside plans:publish's table, more than 64 files, local paths in srcset, poster, CSS
    url() or style, leftover external scripts or stylesheets, and a meta CSP, under
    --lint-only too. The runtime is inlined once from pack's own folder, and the output goes
    beside the input and never over it.
0006-pack-cli.patch
    Parses pack's arguments with node:util parseArgs in strict mode: --root (repeatable),
    -o/--out, --lint-only, --quiet, --help, -- and exactly one input. A syntax error exits
    2 and a validation error exits 1, and neither writes anything. Removes --artifact and
    its second output, for the claude.ai Artifact tool. There is one target, so there is
    no --target flag either.
0007-changes-label.patch
    Gives doc-changes a plain-text label attribute. With no label it reads "Proposed", an
    empty label draws none, and any other value is set as a text node, never as markup, so
    a walkthrough can say "Landed". Zero counts still hide the element. The pure view is
    exported as HtmlPlan.changesView for the smoke.
0008-quote-links.patch
    Opens a doc-quote's link in the same frame, with rel="noopener noreferrer" and no
    target, after writing the state to the URL, so Back returns to it. The viewer's sandbox
    allows no popup and no top-level navigation, so upstream's target="_blank" was a dead
    click. Only http and https links render, by the URL parser's reading of the scheme;
    anything else is plain text. The check is exported as HtmlPlan.safeHref for the smoke.
0009-copy-out.patch
    Shows the response in the Respond sheet in a readonly, selectable textarea. "Copied"
    appears only after navigator.clipboard.writeText resolves or execCommand('copy')
    returns true; upstream said "Copied" whatever execCommand returned. Otherwise the
    textarea is focused and selected, with instructions to copy by hand. The sheet and the
    comment box name no host, and the unused Send path goes.
0010-reading-mode.patch
    Makes data-feedback="off" a reading mode for the walkthrough and report kinds. Upstream
    hid the Respond bar only after every comment control existed. Now the runtime decides
    the mode before it builds any block, and the page draws no comment, strike, draft-edit
    or schema-edit control and no Respond, marks nothing seen, restores no payload and
    writes only a plain #id to the URL. Claims, code, pins, zoom, machine demos and a
    diagram node's detail still work.
-----END PATCHES-----

RE-SYNCING
----------

    1. Check out the upstream repository at the new commit in a scratch directory.
    2. In a fresh, empty scratch tree R, copy each upstream file to its pristine path
       from the path map.
    3. Update the commit SHA, the URL and the PRISTINE SHA-256 lines above from R
       (`sha256sum` on each pristine path), and the upstream LICENSE SHA-256 and the
       Apache-2.0 text below from upstream's LICENSE.
    4. From R, `git apply` each patch in the list above, in order. Regenerate any patch
       that stops applying: rebuild the state it applies to, redo the change on top of it,
       and `git diff --full-index -M` the two states with `a/plugins/plans/...` paths.
       Never hand-edit a patch.
    5. Copy R's plugins/plans/skills/doc/ over this plugin's skills/doc/, leaving the
       first-party skills/doc/SKILL.md alone, and delete any vendored file R does not hold.
    6. Run `node plugins/plans/scripts/smoke-plans.mjs`.

VERIFYING
---------

The patches are ordinary `git diff` output with `a/plugins/plans/...` paths, so apply them
from the root of a repository-shaped tree. Run git apply with GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES set to
the tree's parent, so git never adopts an enclosing repository, and with no --3way, -C,
--unidiff-zero or whitespace option, so nothing is fuzzed.

    Forward: lay out a fresh upstream copy by the path map in R, `sha256sum -c` the ledger,
    `git apply` the patches in order, then `diff -r` R/plugins/plans/skills/doc against
    plugins/plans/skills/doc with -x SKILL.md. They must be byte-identical, else it is wrong.

    Reverse: copy the shipped vendored files into R, `git apply -R` the patches in
    descending order, and `sha256sum -c` the ledger. The file set must equal the ledger.

`node plugins/plans/scripts/smoke-plans.mjs` runs the reverse and then the forward pass on
the shipped tree, with no upstream checkout and no network.

